- Opening: `opening_balance_post` accepts a new section `money` [{money_account_id, amount}] (Dr the account's own chart account). After an opening exists a new account with a figure is refused (`opening_exists_use_topup`): fund it with an owner top-up or a transfer.
- Payment source on 14 event types (salary payment, salary advance, 10-2 voucher, quick expense, supplier payment, purchase payment, owner top-up, owner draw, partner capital / loan, partner profit payout, customer refund, supplier refund, customer advance and its refund, cash handover). `money_event_settings` per event: default source, allow override yes / no, require source yes / no (all off / empty by default). The account travels in the payment itself: text `ma#<id>;` in front of the free text field (wallet, ref or note column; offline-safe, no new parameter on any old function) or `money_account_id` inside the 10-2 form data. A BEFORE INSERT trigger checks it (unknown, inactive, other place, fixed by setting, required), sets the payment mode from the account kind, clears the tag, and checks the negative balance policy. The journal line uses mapping key `m_acct_<id>` so the line hits exactly that account;
